     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose. An overdose like this raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
