       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. No standard indication supports it, and it carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. Normal kidney function doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose you choose.\n- **Enter the order with a note for pharmacy review**, if you have a specific rationale such as a protocol or attending direction. Give me the rationale and I'll put it in the note. I'd still recommend talking to pharmacy or your attending before it's active.\n\nIf the number came from a typo or a mix-up between total daily and per-dose amounts, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
